Two things happened in payments this week

Meridian Pay raised $60 million at a $700 million valuation, led by Foundry Lane.
The company processes about $4 billion of volume a year.

Separately, the central bank published its long-awaited consultation on instant
settlement. Responses are due in November, and the industry expects the rules to
land in the first half of next year.

Both stories point the same way: the plumbing is finally getting attention.

